cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "An improved upper bound for the univalent Bloch-Landau constant: slit domain, certificate programs and paper"
abstract: "A disc with 24 slits, 18 of them curved, together with a computer-assisted proof (exact integer arithmetic and Arb ball arithmetic) that its ratio of inradius to conformal radius is less than 0.65628589. This gives an upper bound for the univalent Bloch-Landau constant below the previously best known values 0.6563937 (Carroll and Ortega-Cerda, 2009) and 0.656319277 (Ortega-Cerda and Pridhnani, 2010). Includes the certificate programs, the data they use, the search and verification code, independent checks, and the paper."
authors:
  - family-names: "van Staden"
    given-names: "Wynand"
type: software
version: "1.0.1"
date-released: "2026-10-14"
license: MIT
